  "reference": "CLABSI per central-line-day across 15 ICUs on an up funnel: Spiegelhalter 2005 section 5 additive random effects drawn exactly as Poisson-gamma, the same model as oep with exposure in place of expected events. phi-hat = 1.223655, tau-hat = 0.001016 per line-day; ucl[0] = 0.023071 at 310 line-days. Cross-checked against an independent numpy + scipy.stats implementation of the whole chain (center line, Pearson residuals, winsorizing, method-of-moments tau^2, and the interpolated quantile of scipy's distribution) to ~1e-11. Upper contours sit at the exact one-sided test's boundary, one count beyond the interpolated quantile, so a point is beyond either line exactly when its exact p-value is below that line's tail probability (docs/methods.md \u00a74.1).",
